==============================================================================
1. KP2 -- log v_inf vs log M (per object; mass PROXIED by luminosity)
==============================================================================
  N = 11 v_blue,95% values: min 145, max 1130 km/s; max/min = 7.79 (0.89 dex); sd(log v) = 0.263 dex
  registered band 350-588 km/s: 6/11 inside; above: ['JADES-GN-68797', 'RUBIES-EGS-42046', 'RUBIES-EGS-49140']; below: ['FRESCO-GN-15498', 'The Cliff']
  registered spread across the stack mass band: x1.68 (M^1/4) vs x4.5 (M^1/2)

  NO Gamma-free per-object mass exists.  Proxy: M ∝ L/Gamma with Gamma held constant
  (this is the framework's own KP2 premise: T pinned + log g mass-independent => Gamma
  fixed => L ∝ M, R_phot ∝ sqrt(M)).  Under that premise d log v/d log L = the KP2 slope.
  L_Halpha tracks L_bol with ~0.2 dex scatter (de Graaff+ 2026) -> sigma_x = 0.2 dex used
  for the attenuation correction.  If Gamma varies with L, these slopes are NOT M-slopes.

  cross-match Naidu x Zenodo (<1", use_dG26): 8/11 matched (FRESCO-GN-9771, GN-15498, JADES-GN-38147 absent from the DJA PRISM catalogue)
