2. KP3 -- T_eff vs n_H against the repo's Saha front
==============================================================================
   Saha front: n_H = 1e+09 cm^-3 -> T_front = 5572 K
   Saha front: n_H = 1e+10 cm^-3 -> T_front = 6037 K
   Saha front: n_H = 1e+11 cm^-3 -> T_front = 6584 K
   Saha front: n_H = 1e+12 cm^-3 -> T_front = 7236 K

  per-object (T_eff, n_H) pairs: NONE PUBLISHED -> the KP3 correlation test CANNOT RUN.
  stack-level T_eff (no n_H attached) vs the curve:
   Median    T_eff 4662 K: below T_front by 910 K (n=1e9) .. 2574 K (n=1e12); Saha-equivalent n_H = 10^6.48 cm^-3
   Luminous  T_eff 4757 K: below T_front by 815 K (n=1e9) .. 2479 K (n=1e12); Saha-equivalent n_H = 10^6.79 cm^-3
   Inter     T_eff 4716 K: below T_front by 856 K (n=1e9) .. 2520 K (n=1e12); Saha-equivalent n_H = 10^6.66 cm^-3
   Faint     T_eff 4233 K: below T_front by 1339 K (n=1e9) .. 3003 K (n=1e12); Saha-equivalent n_H = 10^4.93 cm^-3
   Egg (Liu+26; PHOTOSPHERIC model density, not the CLOUDY layer n_H): rho_ph 7e-12 g/cc -> n_H = 3.0e+12; T_front = 7593 K vs T_eff 4506 K
  (the absolute offset below the front was pre-conceded in R-F1; only the per-object SLOPE
   T_eff(n_H) is a test, and it needs per-object n_H that do not exist.)

