3. R-F3 -- Gamma = kappa_es sigma T^4 / (c g)  (stacks + the one per-object fit)
==============================================================================
  repo reproduction (median stack, log g -2.2 +- 0.2, kappa 0.40): Gamma = 56.6 in [36, 90]

  kappa_es = 0.40 cm^2/g
   Median    T 4662 logg -2.2: Gamma =   56.6  [ 35.3,   91.9]   (L/L_Edd(M_grav) =   50.5)  in [36,90]: True
   Luminous  T 4757 logg -2.5: Gamma =  122.5  [ 95.7,  159.1]   (L/L_Edd(M_grav) =  126.8)  in [36,90]: False
   Inter     T 4716 logg -1.9: Gamma =   29.7  [  3.6,   77.1]   (L/L_Edd(M_grav) =   31.9)  in [36,90]: False
   Faint     T 4233 logg -2.5: Gamma =   76.8  [ 37.7,  156.6]   (L/L_Edd(M_grav) =  100.7)  in [36,90]: True
   Egg (1 obj) T 4506 logg -2.86: Gamma =  226.0  [156.7,  289.8]  sensitivity runs 188-272  in [36,90]: False

  kappa_es = 0.34 cm^2/g
   Median    T 4662 logg -2.2: Gamma =   48.1  [ 30.0,   78.1]   (L/L_Edd(M_grav) =   42.9)  in [36,90]: True
   Luminous  T 4757 logg -2.5: Gamma =  104.1  [ 81.3,  135.2]   (L/L_Edd(M_grav) =  107.8)  in [36,90]: False
   Inter     T 4716 logg -1.9: Gamma =   25.3  [  3.1,   65.5]   (L/L_Edd(M_grav) =   27.1)  in [36,90]: False
   Faint     T 4233 logg -2.5: Gamma =   65.3  [ 32.1,  133.1]   (L/L_Edd(M_grav) =   85.6)  in [36,90]: True
   Egg (1 obj) T 4506 logg -2.86: Gamma =  192.1  [133.2,  246.3]  sensitivity runs 160-231  in [36,90]: False

  kappa 0.40: stack central Gamma span 29.7-122.5; 2/4 stacks inside [36,90]; median-stack Gamma 56.6 vs the paper's dial cap 50 (above); from Table-4 rounded mass: 50.5

  kappa 0.34: stack central Gamma span 25.3-104.1; 2/4 stacks inside [36,90]; median-stack Gamma 48.1 vs the paper's dial cap 50 (below); from Table-4 rounded mass: 42.9

  caveats: (i) g is the NET gravity g - g_dyn (Sun+ Sec.2.2), so this is a net-gravity
  Gamma; an outflow inflates g and deflates Gamma.  (ii) stacks are medians of 15-85
  objects -- the per-object spread is at least as wide and is NOT measurable from the
  public data.  (iii) the Egg is a z~0.1 LRD outside the 117 and its fit includes host +
  dust components.

